  "final_message": "I've built the blog API and frontend on top of the starter project. Most of it is checked; two things are not: I couldn't build or run the Docker image because Docker isn't installed here, and I didn't click through the web pages in a browser.\n\n**What was checked:**\n- Backend tests in `tests/test_api.py` pass. They cover sign-up and sign-in, rejected requests without a valid token, posting and validation errors, search, the tag and author filters, paging, authors-only editing and deleting, and admin take-down and restore. They also check that admin sign-in fails when `ADMIN_PASSWORD` isn't set.\n- Running the backend under gunicorn with 4 workers, the health check, the API and the frontend all respond. Pages like `/posts/3` load correctly.\n- The frontend type-checks and `npm run build` succeeds. `npm ci` works with the updated lock file. The backend's dependencies didn't change.\n\n**Behaviour you might not expect:**\n- **Excerpt:** I take the first 200 characters and then turn line breaks into spaces, so a line break counts toward the 200. If you meant the other order, it's a one-line change in `backend/app.py` (`make_excerpt`).\n- **Account rules:** usernames must be 3\u201364 characters (letters, digits, `_ . -`) and are case-insensitive. Passwords must be 6\u2013128 characters. Nobody can register as `admin`.\n- **Post limits:** titles up to 200 characters, content up to 50,000, and at most 10 tags of up to 32 characters each. Duplicate tags are dropped regardless of case.\n- **Other API responses:**\n  - Changing someone else's post returns 403.\n  - A taken-down post returns 404 even to its own author.\n  - Search matches the title, content and tags.\n  - `page_size` is capped at 100.\n  - Validation errors return 400 with a message for each field, which the editor displays.\n- **Admin password:** it's read each time the app starts. Changing it signs out existing admin sessions, and unsetting it disables the admin account.\n\n**What I added beyond the spec:**\n- `POST /api/auth/logout` and `GET /api/auth/me`.\n- A `taken_down` field on every post.\n- An admin-only \"show taken-down posts\" option in the list, so the admin can find and restore them.\n\nThe frontend uses a small hand-written router rather than adding a routing library. I also added a `.gitignore`, a TypeScript config, a `typecheck` script and a short section in `README.md`.\n\nTo run the tests: `pip install pytest && pytest tests`. To type-check the frontend: `npm run typecheck` in `frontend/`.",
  "final_message_truncated": false,
